# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Cara mengira sempadan tersuai untuk versi terkini Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds"
msgstr "Cara mengira sempadan tersuai"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/custom-bounds.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`compute_forward_bounds` and `compute_backward_bounds` are convenience wrappers. Both are built from\n"
"the same three pieces, which the public API exposes:\n"
msgstr ""
"`compute_forward_bounds` dan `compute_backward_bounds` ialah pembalut kemudahan. Kedua-duanya dibina daripada\n"
"tiga bahagian yang sama, yang didedahkan oleh API awam:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **norm function**, which bounds a single evolved Pauli error term\n"
msgstr "**Fungsi norma**, yang membatasi satu sebutan ralat Pauli yang telah berevolusi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **light cone**, which seeds what the error terms are evolved toward\n"
msgstr "**Kon cahaya**, yang menyemai ke arah mana sebutan ralat dikembangkan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_bounds`, which iterates the circuit and distributes the per-term work\n"
msgstr "`compute_bounds`, yang mengulangi litar dan mengagihkan kerja bagi setiap sebutan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assembling them yourself means you can bound something the wrappers don't cover. This guide works\n"
"through one case where that is worth doing: a **mirror circuit**, where the usual backward bound is\n"
"needlessly loose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memasangnya sendiri bermaksud anda boleh membatasi sesuatu yang tidak dilindungi oleh pembalut. Panduan ini menunjukkan\n"
"satu kes yang berbaloi dilakukan: **litar cermin**, di mana sempadan belakang yang biasa\n"
"terlalu longgar tanpa keperluan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the wrappers actually do {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"
msgstr "Apa yang sebenarnya dilakukan oleh pembalut {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two wrappers differ in the three places listed above:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua pembalut berbeza pada tiga tempat yang disenaraikan di atas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| circuit | as given | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| norm function | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, against the observable | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, against the initial state |\n"
"| light cone | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, seeded from the observable | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, seeded from every active qubit |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| litar | seperti yang diberikan | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| fungsi norma | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, terhadap observabel | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, terhadap keadaan awal |\n"
"| kon cahaya | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, disemai daripada observabel | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, disemai daripada setiap qubit aktif |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The forward bound asks *\"How much can this error change the observable I am about to measure?\"* and\n"
"answers it with the spectral norm of a commutator. The backward bound asks *\"How much can this error\n"
"change the state I started from?\"* and answers with a nuclear norm, taking that state to be the\n"
"all-zero state on every active qubit. They are different questions, and each is the right one for\n"
"errors in its own half of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan hadapan bertanya *\"Sejauh mana ralat ini boleh mengubah observabel yang akan saya ukur?\"* dan\n"
"menjawabnya dengan norma spektrum bagi komutator. Sempadan belakang bertanya *\"Sejauh mana ralat ini boleh\n"
"mengubah keadaan yang saya mulakan?\"* dan menjawab dengan norma nuklear, dengan mengambil keadaan itu sebagai\n"
"keadaan semua-sifar pada setiap qubit aktif. Ini soalan yang berbeza, dan setiap satu ialah yang tepat bagi\n"
"ralat dalam separuhnya sendiri daripada litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mirror circuit case {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"
msgstr "Kes litar cermin {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mirror circuit applies some unitary and then undoes it: $U^\\dagger U$. These appear whenever\n"
"the ideal outcome has to be known exactly (generally Loschmidt echoes, randomized benchmarking, and\n"
"verification experiments).\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar cermin menggunakan suatu uniter dan kemudian membatalkannya: $U^\\dagger U$. Ia muncul apabila\n"
"hasil ideal mesti diketahui dengan tepat (umumnya gema Loschmidt, penanda aras rawak, dan\n"
"eksperimen pengesahan).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mirror circuits have a property the generic backward bound cannot exploit. Because the second half\n"
"is the inverse of the first, *evolving an error backward to the initial state* traverses the same\n"
"gates as *evolving it forward to the observable*. The two questions coincide, so the sharper\n"
"forward-style bound is valid for the backward direction too.\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar cermin mempunyai sifat yang tidak dapat dieksploitasi oleh sempadan belakang generik. Oleh kerana separuh kedua\n"
"ialah songsangan separuh pertama, *mengembangkan ralat ke belakang menuju keadaan awal* melalui get yang sama\n"
"seperti *mengembangkannya ke hadapan menuju observabel*. Kedua-dua soalan itu bertepatan, jadi sempadan\n"
"gaya hadapan yang lebih tajam adalah sah untuk arah belakang juga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the custom bound {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"
msgstr "Pasang sempadan tersuai {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recipe keeps what `compute_backward_bounds` does with the circuit (strip the measurements,\n"
"invert it, and iterate it with `backwards=True`) and substitutes the other two pieces: the forward\n"
"norm function, and a light cone seeded from the observable with `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"exactly as `compute_forward_bounds` seeds its own. Each substitution is one line.\n"
msgstr ""
"Resipi ini mengekalkan apa yang dilakukan oleh `compute_backward_bounds` terhadap litar (membuang pengukuran,\n"
"menyongsangkannya, dan mengulanginya dengan `backwards=True`) dan menggantikan dua bahagian lain: fungsi\n"
"norma hadapan, dan kon cahaya yang disemai daripada observabel dengan `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"tepat seperti `compute_forward_bounds` menyemai kon cahayanya sendiri. Setiap penggantian ialah satu baris.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much it gains {#how-much-it-gains}"
msgstr "Berapa banyak yang diperoleh {#how-much-it-gains}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Comparing against the stock backward bound on the same circuit, summarized the same way as in the\n"
"[configuration guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): the mean bound and its standard deviation,\n"
"followed by the share of terms bounded by 0, with a bound computed in between, and left at the\n"
"trivial 2.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membandingkan dengan sempadan belakang stok pada litar yang sama, diringkaskan dengan cara yang sama seperti dalam\n"
"[panduan konfigurasi](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): purata sempadan dan sisihan piawainya,\n"
"diikuti dengan bahagian sebutan yang dibatasi oleh 0, dengan sempadan yang dikira di antaranya, dan yang kekal pada\n"
"2.0 remeh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The stock backward bound sits near the trivial value of 2.0, which carries almost no information. On\n"
"a mirror circuit, every error is \"close to the initial state\" in the sense that bound measures, so\n"
"it cannot discriminate between terms. The custom bound is several times tighter and bounds many of the terms by 0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan belakang stok berada hampir nilai remeh 2.0, yang hampir tidak membawa maklumat. Pada\n"
"litar cermin, setiap ralat \"dekat dengan keadaan awal\" dalam erti kata yang diukur oleh sempadan itu, jadi\n"
"ia tidak dapat membezakan antara sebutan. Sempadan tersuai beberapa kali lebih ketat dan membatasi banyak sebutan dengan 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To check the implementation, the two can be compared box by box. For every box, the\n"
"custom backward bound comes out **identical** to that same box's forward bound, up to rounding\n"
"error. Both bound the same error at the same point in the circuit, and on a mirror circuit the gates\n"
"after that point cancel to the inverse of the gates before it, so the two computations evaluate the\n"
"same quantity from opposite ends:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyemak pelaksanaan, kedua-duanya boleh dibandingkan kotak demi kotak. Bagi setiap kotak,\n"
"sempadan belakang tersuai keluar **sama** dengan sempadan hadapan kotak yang sama itu, sehingga ralat\n"
"pembundaran. Kedua-duanya membatasi ralat yang sama pada titik yang sama dalam litar, dan pada litar cermin get\n"
"selepas titik itu membatal menjadi songsangan get sebelumnya, jadi kedua-dua pengiraan menilai\n"
"kuantiti yang sama dari hujung yang bertentangan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** This equality is a property of the mirror structure, not of the technique. On a circuit\n"
"that is not self-inverting, the same substitution still runs but no longer computes a *valid* bound\n"
"for the backward direction: it answers the forward question about a circuit half where that\n"
"question does not apply. **Only use this when the second half of your circuit inverts the\n"
"first.**\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** Kesamaan ini ialah sifat struktur cermin, bukan teknik tersebut. Pada litar yang\n"
"bukan songsang-diri, penggantian yang sama masih berjalan tetapi tidak lagi mengira sempadan *sah*\n"
"untuk arah belakang: ia menjawab soalan hadapan tentang separuh litar di mana\n"
"soalan itu tidak terpakai. **Gunakan ini hanya apabila separuh kedua litar anda menyongsangkan\n"
"yang pertama.**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</div>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed it into the rest of the workflow {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Salurkan ke dalam aliran kerja selebihnya {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is an ordinary `Bounds` dictionary, so everything that follows is unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya ialah kamus `Bounds` biasa, jadi semua yang mengikutinya tidak berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a mirror circuit there is also no reason to compute either bound for the whole circuit. The\n"
"forward bounds are only needed for the boxes of $U^\\dagger$, counted from the end, and the backward\n"
"bounds only for the boxes of $U$, counted from the start. `max_num_boxes` therefore limits each of\n"
"them to half of the noisy boxes, and `merge_bounds` joins the two halves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada litar cermin juga tiada sebab untuk mengira kedua-dua sempadan bagi keseluruhan litar. Sempadan\n"
"hadapan hanya diperlukan untuk kotak $U^\\dagger$, dikira dari hujung, dan sempadan belakang\n"
"hanya untuk kotak $U$, dikira dari permulaan. Oleh itu `max_num_boxes` menghadkan setiap satunya\n"
"kepada separuh daripada kotak bising, dan `merge_bounds` menggabungkan kedua-dua separuh itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is how the bounds are used in practice, and it means the box-for-box comparison above is no\n"
"longer available: it needs both bounds for every box. It is a check of the implementation for this guide, not workflow step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beginilah sempadan digunakan dalam amalan, dan ini bermakna perbandingan kotak demi kotak di atas tidak\n"
"lagi tersedia: ia memerlukan kedua-dua sempadan bagi setiap kotak. Ia semakan pelaksanaan untuk panduan ini, bukan langkah aliran kerja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the stock backward bounds, the sampling overhead is far larger. `merge_bounds` uses the\n"
"backward bounds up to one switch point in the circuit and the forward bounds from there on,\n"
"choosing the point that minimizes the total bias. With each bound computed for one half, that point\n"
"falls in the middle of the circuit, so the boxes of $U$ are covered by backward bounds alone. The\n"
"stock backward bound is close to the trivial 2.0 there, which drives the overhead up. The custom\n"
"one is as tight as the forward bound would have been, so the overhead matches that of the complete\n"
"forward bounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan sempadan belakang stok, overhed persampelan jauh lebih besar. `merge_bounds` menggunakan\n"
"sempadan belakang sehingga satu titik pensuisan dalam litar dan sempadan hadapan dari situ seterusnya,\n"
"memilih titik yang meminimumkan jumlah pincang. Dengan setiap sempadan dikira untuk satu separuh, titik itu\n"
"jatuh di tengah litar, jadi kotak $U$ dilindungi oleh sempadan belakang sahaja. Sempadan\n"
"belakang stok hampir 2.0 remeh di situ, yang menaikkan overhed. Yang tersuai\n"
"sama ketat seperti sempadan hadapan, jadi overhed sepadan dengan overhed sempadan\n"
"hadapan yang lengkap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That raises the obvious question of why to bother, when the complete forward bounds alone give the\n"
"same result. The answer is cost. A forward bound for a box early in the circuit evolves its error\n"
"through the rest of $U$ and then all of $U^\\dagger$, which is the longest and widest evolution in\n"
"the circuit. The evolved operator can grow exponentially in the number of non-Clifford gates\n"
"it passes through, and computing the commutator's spectral norm gets exponentially more expensive as\n"
"the light cone widens. In the half-and-half approach, no error is evolved through more than half of\n"
"the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Itu menimbulkan soalan yang jelas mengapa perlu bersusah payah, apabila sempadan hadapan lengkap sahaja memberikan\n"
"hasil yang sama. Jawapannya ialah kos. Sempadan hadapan bagi kotak awal dalam litar mengembangkan ralatnya\n"
"melalui baki $U$ dan kemudian keseluruhan $U^\\dagger$, iaitu evolusi terpanjang dan terlebar dalam\n"
"litar. Operator yang telah berevolusi boleh bertambah secara eksponen dalam bilangan get bukan Clifford\n"
"yang dilaluinya, dan mengira norma spektrum komutator menjadi semakin mahal secara eksponen apabila\n"
"kon cahaya melebar. Dalam pendekatan separuh-separuh, tiada ralat dikembangkan melalui lebih daripada separuh\n"
"litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The saving therefore grows with the circuit depth. More importantly, the complete forward\n"
"bounds stop being computable long before the halfway ones do. Once the evolutions of the early\n"
"boxes exceed `evolution_max_terms` or `eigval_max_qubits`, their bounds are truncated or fall back\n"
"to the triangle inequality, and eventually they cost too much to compute. Wherever that point\n"
"lies, the half-and-half approach only needs it to fall somewhere in the first half of the circuit.\n"
"The forward bounds have to reach no further than the middle, and on a mirror circuit, the backward\n"
"bounds for the boxes of $U$ evolve their errors back to the start through as much of the\n"
"circuit as the forward bounds for the matching boxes of $U^\\dagger$ do to the end, so they run out\n"
"at the same depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penjimatan itu oleh itu bertambah dengan kedalaman litar. Lebih penting lagi, sempadan hadapan\n"
"lengkap tidak lagi boleh dikira jauh lebih awal daripada yang separuh. Apabila evolusi kotak\n"
"awal melebihi `evolution_max_terms` atau `eigval_max_qubits`, sempadannya dipangkas atau beralih\n"
"kepada ketaksamaan segi tiga, dan akhirnya ia terlalu mahal untuk dikira. Di mana pun titik itu\n"
"terletak, pendekatan separuh-separuh hanya memerlukannya jatuh di suatu tempat dalam separuh pertama litar.\n"
"Sempadan hadapan tidak perlu sampai lebih jauh daripada tengah, dan pada litar cermin, sempadan\n"
"belakang bagi kotak $U$ mengembangkan ralatnya kembali ke permulaan melalui litar sebanyak\n"
"sempadan hadapan bagi kotak $U^\\dagger$ yang sepadan hingga ke hujung, jadi ia kehabisan\n"
"pada kedalaman yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** Why compute backward bounds for the boxes of $U$, when the forward bounds of the\n"
"boxes of $U^\\dagger$ look like they should hold the same numbers? Because the boxes are not mirror\n"
"images of each other. Each box injects its noise on one side of its gates, and the inverse layers of\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ are separate boxes with noise models of their own, so the box that mirrors a box of $U$\n"
"sees its errors at a different point in the circuit. Therefore, their bounds only partly agree, and\n"
"the bounds for the boxes of $U$ have to be computed for those boxes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** Mengapa mengira sempadan belakang bagi kotak $U$, apabila sempadan hadapan bagi\n"
"kotak $U^\\dagger$ nampaknya patut mempunyai nombor yang sama? Kerana kotak-kotak itu bukan imej cermin\n"
"bagi satu sama lain. Setiap kotak menyuntik hingarnya pada satu sisi get-getnya, dan lapisan songsang\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ ialah kotak berasingan dengan model hingar tersendiri, jadi kotak yang mencerminkan kotak $U$\n"
"melihat ralatnya pada titik yang berbeza dalam litar. Oleh itu, sempadannya hanya sebahagian sepadan, dan\n"
"sempadan bagi kotak $U$ mesti dikira untuk kotak-kotak tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing other custom bounds {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"
msgstr "Menulis sempadan tersuai yang lain {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same three substitutions cover other cases:\n"
msgstr "Tiga penggantian yang sama merangkumi kes lain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm.** `time_evolved_norm_forward` accepts `comm_norm_order`; passing anything\n"
"other than `2` skips the eigensolver and computes that norm directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Norma yang berbeza.** `time_evolved_norm_forward` menerima `comm_norm_order`; memasukkan apa-apa\n"
"selain `2` melangkau penyelesai eigen dan mengira norma itu secara terus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different light cone.** `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` seeds a light cone from any Pauli,\n"
"and the `LightCone` constructor takes the qubits to track and the operations seeding it, so a\n"
"bound can be computed against any operator you can express that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kon cahaya yang berbeza.** `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` menyemai kon cahaya daripada sebarang Pauli,\n"
"dan pembina `LightCone` menerima qubit yang hendak dijejak dan operasi yang menyemainya, jadi\n"
"sempadan boleh dikira terhadap sebarang operator yang anda boleh ungkapkan dengan cara itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm function entirely.** `compute_bounds` only requires a callable: taking a\n"
"`Pauli` and `RotationGates` and returning a `CommutatorBounds`. Anything satisfying that signature\n"
"works, including a closed-form bound specific to your circuit family.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fungsi norma yang sama sekali berbeza.** `compute_bounds` hanya memerlukan satu callable: yang menerima\n"
"`Pauli` dan `RotationGates` serta mengembalikan `CommutatorBounds`. Apa sahaja yang memenuhi tandatangan itu\n"
"berfungsi, termasuk sempadan bentuk-tertutup khusus untuk keluarga litar anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whatever you substitute, you must prove that the result is a genuine upper bound.\n"
"Understating an error term's effect does not produce a visible failure. It produces an expectation\n"
"value that is quietly wrong, because the term will have been dropped from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa sahaja yang anda gantikan, anda mesti membuktikan bahawa hasilnya ialah sempadan atas yang tulen.\n"
"Memperkecilkan kesan sesuatu sebutan ralat tidak menghasilkan kegagalan yang kelihatan. Ia menghasilkan nilai\n"
"jangkaan yang salah secara senyap, kerana sebutan itu akan telah digugurkan daripada model hingar yang dimitigasi.\n"
